<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian housing finance fell 6.9 pct in Feb.</title>
<headline>Australian housing finance fell 6.9 pct in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance commitments for owner-occupied housing in Australia fell 6.9 percent by volume to 39,457 dwellings in February from a January level of 42,403, seasonally-adjusted, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>In value terms, housing finance fell to A$4.13 billion in February from A$4.61 billion in January, the bureau said. </p>
<p>Australian housing finance, February 1997 -</p>
<p>    Dwelling commitments	Feb 97     Jan 97	Feb 96</p>
<p>    Seasonally-adjusted	 39,457     42,403	39,582</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		    38,760     35,868	40,817</p>
<p>    Trend			   40,363     40,339	38,507</p>
<p>Value (A$ billion)</p>
<p>    Seasonally-adjusted	  4.13	 4.61	  3.81</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		     4.03	 3.76	  3.88</p>
<p>    Trend estimates		4.30	 4.25	  3.74</p>
<p>The bureau said finance commitments for the construction of new dwellings fell 1.1 percent and commitments for the purchase of established dwellings fell 7.5 percent.</p>
<p>The bureau said the number of commitments under new finance, excluding refinancing, fell by 5.8 percent.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
